		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Battery voltage percentage fluctuation]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=83&amp;p=36306#p36306"><![CDATA[
Joined here last week, &amp; looking through old posts to learn what I can. Just got a DM1701 made in 2024. Has FW 20241215, &amp; CPU TYT. After a full charge, the display shows the battery at 100%, &amp; 8.2 volts. Using a Fluke multimeter measuring the battery voltage when it comes off the charger at the contacts that power the radio, the voltage is 8.27. I was considering the TP5100 upgrade, but the original charger  doesn’t seem to overcharge the battery, &amp; both the charger, &amp; battery stay cool. Sure it’s slow, but I have other radios I can use while this one is charging. So I think your charging parameters are right on. Who knows, maybe the mfr changed some components to lower the voltage due to feedback. Again, thanks for all you did to make these radios so much better. GARY. N4KVE<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8235">N4KVE</a> — Thu Mar 20, 2025 11:50 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
